// A top-level statement calls a `fn` declared textually LATER in the file. The checker hoists every
// top-level declaration (collect.rs pass 1), so the forward reference type-checks; the runtime must
// agree by binding all top-level `fn`s before the statement sequence runs — the same hoist that
// already lets fn bodies and mutually-recursive fns forward-reference. Previously this aborted with
// a runtime E0005 ("cannot find `greet`"), a checker/runtime mismatch.
// expect: stdout "hello"
// expect: exit 0
echo greet()
fn greet(): string {
    return "hello";
}
